The registry-first sample tests/registry/br.jsonl contains street names, numbers, localities,
CEPs and coordinates from CNEFE (Cadastro Nacional de Endereços para Fins Estatísticos),
2022 Demographic Census release with address coordinates, published by IBGE (Instituto
Brasileiro de Geografia e Estatística). Source: IBGE, Censo Demográfico 2022, CNEFE,
https://www.ibge.gov.br/estatisticas/sociais/populacao/38734-cadastro-nacional-de-enderecos-para-fins-estatisticos.html
and https://ftp.ibge.gov.br/Cadastro_Nacional_de_Enderecos_para_Fins_Estatisticos/Censo_Demografico_2022/Arquivos_CNEFE/CSV/UF/
IBGE states no licence for these files; data published by the Brazilian federal Executive are
free to use under Decree 8.777/2016, art. 4 (as amended by Decree 9.903/2019), crediting the
source. Municipality names and state abbreviations come from IBGE's localidades API
(https://servicodados.ibge.gov.br/api/v1/localidades/municipios), fetched on 2026-10-22.
Queries were constructed from registry fields joined with that list; coordinates are the
registry's SIRGAS 2000 latitude/longitude, unchanged. Per-case prepared-CSV checksums are
recorded in the corpus; docs/evaluation/registry/br.md records the upstream checksums.
